Z||000000||zeusrekning||05-08-2000||10:00 PM||||Yes i know this is a bad ? but i never know what to put for the subject. I am considering looking for another fiero. A v6 4speed what year and model should i look for?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||05-08-2000||10:16 PM||||I love the GT's.  Save yourself  some money and buy an 86 or 87.  The 88 although better in the suspension can be expensive to fix because parts are scarse.  86 or 87 GT's suspensions can be converted inexpensively and in most cases end up better then the 88's.  I know some will disagree with me, but that's my view.  Happy hunting!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||05-08-2000||10:20 PM||||The pre 86 V6 had the four speed. The 86 1/2 went to the five speed (much better choice [my opinion])<P>Remember the newest Fiero is 12 years old and unless it has been well maintained it take$ $$$$$$ to fix.||||reg||1
Z||000003||zeusrekning||05-08-2000||10:23 PM||||So you recomend a 5 speed. My 87 4cyl is a 5 speed. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeusrekning||05-08-2000||10:23 PM||||So you recomend a 5 speed. My 87 4cyl is a 5 speed. Scared of more clutch problems how reliable are the automatics?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||05-08-2000||10:54 PM||||I just sold an 85 SE and now have an 88GT. I could not tell that much difference between them, other than the 88 has a smoother ride. I like the 88's because of the refinement, but replacement parts are tougher to find. An 87 SE with the v6 and 5 speed would be a good choice. The clutches do give trouble, but with some preventative (did I make that word up??) stuff like new fluid, the system does work. I can't imagine driving an automatic Fiero- the manual tranny's are so much fun to drive.||||reg||1
Z||000006||wkayl||05-08-2000||11:05 PM||||The best year????<P>Whatever you own.....||||reg||1
Z||000007||RobertVol||05-08-2000||11:09 PM||||Will have to say I prefer the the 88's BUT..!<P>Actually there was some refinement in the the 88's but try but like they said...^  try replacing some of the parts on the 88. <P>Like the aluminum calipers on the rear brakes. Yikes! HARD to do if dont want to modify. BUT there was things to like about the pre-88's. Actually the pre -88 were a little quicker Stock on the Gt's. SMOG SoMeTHING ON the 88 model you know BLAH BLAH BLAH. For overall performance I would actually take a low mileage well taken care of 87 GT. A little heavier than a formula BuT looks nicer in my honest opinion. and does not have the as much CAFE restriciton<P>also The 87 had the 5 speed over the 4. Which I prefer but thats only opinion.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Boodoggin||05-08-2000||11:27 PM||||I vote for 86 GT 4 speed.  Ive driven them all.  It still seems to launch better. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||05-09-2000||07:40 AM||||I like my 4 speed just fine. I have never driven the 5 speed, and it would be nice to have that freeway gear, but I have heard scary stories of bad synchros in the 5 speed.||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||05-09-2000||10:02 AM||||I like my 86.5 GT just fine!  Been with me for 11 years, 4 clutchs, 2 tranny's, 3 heater cores, 4 sets of rubber, 1 carpet job, 2 stereos, and 2 damaged front bumpers.<P>Oh, yea, and the car has sat for 4 years... but this week...<P>like the mythical Phoenix, the Pegasus rises from the ashe's!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
